THIRD-PARTY CORPUS ATTRIBUTIONS  (corpus/NOTICE)
================================================

`corpus/` is a PUBLIC repository, so `git push` IS redistribution. The moment the
first external attack set is copied in, the third-party attribution obligation has
ALREADY triggered — not "will trigger later" (EV-COVERAGE-E3 §10.2). This file is
that attribution: one entry per external source, carrying its project / license /
url and — load-bearing — the exact COMMIT that pins what we took.

    未 pin 的署名不是可核验的来源证明。
    An un-pinned attribution is not a verifiable provenance claim.

A `commit` that is empty, all-zeros, `TODO`, `xxxxxxx`, or not a hex sha pins
NOTHING. tools/check_corpus_notice.py reds it even though this file itself states
the principle above — the gate checks that an attribution is MEANINGFUL, not merely
that it EXISTS (查有意义不只查存在, §10.2). A sibling mechanism's bidirectional gate
verified existence but not meaning, and a `0000000` sailed through green; this gate
does not repeat that.

Attribution is enforced BOTH directions by tools/check_corpus_notice.py:
  - a source used by >= 1 corpus case but absent here  =>  build red;
  - a source listed here but used by zero cases         =>  build red.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY FORMAT   (the first external merge fills this in; today there are none)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  [<source-id>]                     # the `source:` prefix before the first ':'
  project:     <name>
  license:     <SPDX id or license name>
  url:         <upstream url>
  commit:      <full hex sha>       # pins EXACTLY what was taken
  license-text:
    <the upstream license / copyright paragraph, verbatim>

  Probe-tool sources (e.g. garak) additionally pin — a probe's OUTPUT changes with
  the tool version, so a bare repo sha does not pin what we exported (§10.2):

  type:        probe-tool
  version:     <tool release, e.g. 0.9.2>
  probe:       <exact probe name, e.g. encoding.InjectBase64>
  export-date: <YYYY-MM-DD the probe corpus was exported>

The sources this repo recognises as external-native are datasets such as deepset /
promptinject and the probe tool garak; the authoritative allowlist lives in
treval.active_eval.coverage.EXTERNAL_NATIVE_SOURCES (this file does not restate it).

