MODIFICATIONS (Apache-2.0 §4(b) "note the changes" / MIT notice retention)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where a taken file was changed, the change is annotated IN PLACE via the case's
`source:` tag suffix — this is where the "You changed the files" notice lives:
  · `(payload-neutralized)` — the harmful payload was swapped for a benign canary;
    the pre-swap upstream string's hash is in the case's `pre_neutralize_hash`
    (the three garak promptinject.Hijack* rows).
  · `(bare-payload-control)` — the injection SKELETON was stripped to form the
    §2.2.3 control arm; the verbatim external payload is retained, the framing removed
    (the 49 control_bare_payload cases; each keeps its partner's external source prefix).
Verbatim rows carry NO such suffix (unchanged). This satisfies Apache-2.0 §4(b) for the
garak/deepset material and preserves the MIT notice for the promptinject rows.

